# interplay_memlive_intermediate_depth3: An intermediate page-table entry rewritten between execs, at depth 2 (the root table's entry 1, which names the last-level table of VA pages 4096-8191) and at depth 3 (entry 1 of the first second-level table, the same VA pages). Buffer A at VA page 4096 is read once; then the guest points the entry at a copy of the table whose leaves for A, for B (never made) and for the command-buffer page 4099 name other pages. The walk reads every table below the root at every walk: the command buffer at 4099 is read from the new page and runs its other copies; A, live, reads its old page; B is made over the copy's leaf. With the entry cleared, A still reads (nothing walks for a live object) and C, never made, faults ("Found a hole in the page table"); with the copy back C is made over it. In the blocks setup a buffer is a lazy map of the host task, which maps whatever the table says when a range is first used.
